**New Evidence**
The 2022 portfolio is clearest on four strands: low-rate-led macro policy, state-directed investment, export-led growth, and high-leverage diplomacy.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"2022 Yılı Cumhurbaşkanlığı Yıllık Programı 25/10/2021 Tarih ve 31639 (Mükerrer) Sayılı Resmi Gazete’de yayımlanmıştır","publisher":"T.C. Cumhurbaşkanlığı Strateji ve Bütçe Başkanlığı","publication_date":"2021-10-26","url":"https://www.sbb.gov.tr/2022-yili-cumhurbaskanligi-yillik-programi-25-10-2021-tarih-ve-31639-mukerrer-sayili-resmi-gazetede-yayimlanmistir/?device=1","claim":"The 2022 Presidential Annual Program set macroeconomic, fiscal, and sectoral policies around a strong and stable economy, competitive production, skilled people, liveable cities, sustainable environment, rule of law, democratization, and good governance, and said the measures would be monitored quarterly.","locator":"official summary paragraph on the program page","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct government planning summary; reliable for the declared framework, but it is aspirational rather than proof of delivery.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Adopted before and governing the 2022 calendar year.","ruler_attribution":"Formally attributable to Erdoğan's presidency and state apparatus; it shows the declared program, not personal authorship line by line.","contrary_evidence":["A planning document does not itself show execution or course correction beyond the stated monitoring mechanism."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.6"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"2022 Yılı Yatırım Programı Yayımlandı","publisher":"T.C. Cumhurbaşkanlığı Strateji ve Bütçe Başkanlığı","publication_date":"2022-01-24","url":"https://www.sbb.gov.tr/2022-yili-yatirim-programi-yayimlandi/","claim":"The 2022 Investment Program, carrying Erdoğan's signature, allocated 184.3 billion TL to 3,134 projects and said priority went to projects with the highest economic and social impact and the most urgent service needs.","locator":"paragraphs reporting the program and the total allocation","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct official investment-program announcement with explicit figures and signature attribution.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"This is the program for 2022 implementation.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable at the formal executive level because the program is described as carrying Erdoğan's signature; completion still needs separate proof.","contrary_evidence":["The allocation shows intent and prioritization, not that every project was completed on schedule."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.4","8B.6","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"2022 Yılı Yatırım Programı Yayımlandı","publisher":"T.C. Cumhurbaşkanlığı Strateji ve Bütçe Başkanlığı","publication_date":"2022-01-24","url":"https://www.sbb.gov.tr/2022-yili-yatirim-programi-yayimlandi/","claim":"The 2022 Investment Program concentrated spending on transport and communications, education, energy, mining, agriculture, health, water and sewerage, and also funded major rail, metro, gas storage, flood control, wildfire, and dam projects.","locator":"sector allocation and project examples in the body of the article","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct official sector allocation and project list; strong evidence of concrete prioritization, though not completion.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 budgetary execution plan and project list.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Erdoğan's government through the formal investment program; it shows what the administration chose to fund.","contrary_evidence":["Sectoral allocations show priorities but do not by themselves prove delivery or impact."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.4","8B.6"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Türkiye Unveils 2022-2024 Medium-Term Program","publisher":"Invest in Türkiye","publication_date":"2021-09-07","url":"https://www.invest.gov.tr/en/news/news-from-turkey/pages/turkey-unveils-2022-2024-medium-term-program.aspx","claim":"Türkiye's 2022-2024 Medium-Term Program set explicit targets for GDP growth, unemployment, inflation, exports, and tourism, and described the program as the tool that initiates the budget process and allocates resources in line with public policies and the Development Plan.","locator":"opening summary paragraphs","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official government investment-office summary of a formal program; good for stated goals and resource-allocation intent, not proof of implementation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Program adopted before 2022 and governing the period under review.","ruler_attribution":"Co-developed by Treasury/Finance and the Strategy and Budget presidency under Erdoğan's administration; attribution is institutional rather than personal.","contrary_evidence":["Targets later proved too optimistic on inflation, so the program is better evidence of intent than of realized control."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Erdogan says interest rates will be lowered and inflation will fall too","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-01-29","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/erdogan-says-interest-rates-will-be-lowered-and-inflation-will-fall-too-2752504","claim":"Erdoğan publicly repeated that interest rates would keep falling and inflation would fall with them; Reuters framed this as part of an economic model engineered by Erdoğan amid a currency crisis.","locator":"article opening paragraphs and quoted remarks","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters reporting is strong for the statement and context, while the policy attribution is still partly inferential.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"January 2022, squarely inside the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable because it quotes Erdoğan's public stance and links the policy line to his repeated intervention in monetary policy.","contrary_evidence":["The article reports a claim and policy stance, not proof that the stance was economically sound or successfully implemented."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.3","8B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Turkey unveils latest salvo against soaring inflation","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-06-10","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/turkey-announces-steps-to-shore-up-economy-prioritising-inflation-fight-2835744","claim":"Türkiye's government launched bank and bond-market measures to cool inflation and stabilise the currency while avoiding higher rates, and Reuters said the inflationary spiral followed central-bank cuts made under pressure from Erdoğan.","locator":"article opening paragraphs and the section headed 'STEPS TAKEN'","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters reporting with concrete policy details and explicit attribution to the low-rate line under Erdoğan.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"June 2022, within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Strongly attributable because the article ties the measures and earlier rate cuts to Erdoğan's policy preference and pressure.","contrary_evidence":["Analysts quoted in the story argued the measures skirted the need to raise rates and might do little to control inflation."],"lenses":["8B.6","8B.8","8B.9","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Press Release on Interest Rates (2022-42)","publisher":"Central Bank of the Republic of Türkiye","publication_date":"2022-10-20","url":"https://tcmb.gov.tr/wps/wcm/connect/en/tcmb%2Ben/main%2Bmenu/announcements/press%2Breleases/2022/ano2022-42","claim":"The Monetary Policy Committee cut the policy rate from 12 percent to 10.5 percent and said it would continue to use liraization, macroprudential tools, and data-driven decisions to support price stability, growth, and employment.","locator":"press release paragraphs 46-59","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary central-bank record of the decision and the stated policy framework; excellent for what was done, though not a direct presidential order record.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"October 2022, within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Formally a central-bank decision, but it aligns with and likely reflects Erdoğan's persistent low-rate line; attribution is moderate rather than absolute.","contrary_evidence":["The central bank is formally independent, so the move is not identical to a personal presidential decree."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.3","8B.6","8B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Financing the Next Generation of Green Growth and Prosperity in Turkey","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-02-28","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/country/turkey/publication/Financing-the-next-generation-of-green-growth-and-prosperity-in-Turkey","claim":"The World Bank said Türkiye had made progress by rapidly increasing renewable energy production and expanding waste-treatment infrastructure, while noting that recent leadership announcements pointed to ambitious climate and resilience plans.","locator":"highlight and summary paragraphs around lines 58-59 and 70-71","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"High-quality World Bank summary of sector progress and leadership signals, though it is partly descriptive rather than audited outcome data.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Published in 2022 and describing the 2022 policy environment.","ruler_attribution":"Leadership announcements are attributable to Erdoğan's administration, but the report does not claim he personally managed each project.","contrary_evidence":["The report also says Türkiye remains resource-intensive and that more progress is still possible."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.6","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Türkiye's Exports Soar to Record USD 254 Billion in 2022","publisher":"Invest in Türkiye","publication_date":"2023-01-08","url":"https://www.invest.gov.tr/en/news/news-from-turkey/pages/turkiye-exports-soar-record-usd-254-billion-2022.aspx","claim":"President Erdoğan announced that exports reached a record 254.2 billion dollars in 2022, rose 12.9 percent year on year, and remained part of his stated goal of putting Türkiye among the world's top 10 exporters.","locator":"opening paragraphs of the article","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official announcement of the reported export figure and stated objective; reliable for the announced result, but causal credit is partly inferential.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective report on 2022 results, published immediately after the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable as a public announcement by Erdoğan, though the export outcome also reflects firms, exchange rates, and global demand.","contrary_evidence":["Export growth was also shaped by external conditions and market dynamics, so the figure does not prove presidential competence by itself."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.7","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Annual Gross Domestic Product - 2022","publisher":"TURKSTAT Data Portal","publication_date":"2023-08-31","url":"https://veriportali.tuik.gov.tr/en/press/49742","claim":"Official Turkish statistics said annual GDP increased by 5.5 percent in 2022 and GDP per capita reached 10,659 US dollars at current prices.","locator":"data-portal summary text in the search snippet","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official statistics are strong for the reported figures, though the page itself is surfaced through a search snippet because the portal is JavaScript-gated.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 outcome report, published after year-end.","ruler_attribution":"Outcome data are attributable to Erdoğan's administration only in part; they also reflect tourism, private-sector activity, war shocks, and the post-pandemic rebound.","contrary_evidence":["The same year also featured very high inflation and currency stress, so growth alone is not a clean competence proxy."],"lenses":["8B.7","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Labour Force Statistics - 2022","publisher":"TURKSTAT Data Portal","publication_date":"2023-03-23","url":"https://veriportali.tuik.gov.tr/en/press/49390","claim":"Official Turkish statistics reported that unemployment fell to 10.4 percent in 2022, employment rose by 2.3 percentage points, and labour-force participation rose to 53.1 percent.","locator":"data-portal summary text in the search snippet","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official labour-market statistics are strong for the reported outcomes, though causation remains shared with the private sector and broader macro conditions.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 outcome report, published after year-end.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to the administration only in a broad sense, because employment responds to tourism, external demand, and the rebound from pandemic disruption.","contrary_evidence":["These gains coexist with severe inflation and real-income erosion, so they do not prove broad policy success."],"lenses":["8B.7","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Black Sea Grain Initiative is renewed","publisher":"United Nations in Türkiye","publication_date":"2022-11-18","url":"https://turkiye.un.org/en/208017-black-sea-grain-initiative-renewed","claim":"The UN said more than 11.1 million tonnes of essential foodstuffs had been shipped under the Black Sea Grain Initiative, and it praised the role of Türkiye and President Erdoğan as the Istanbul channel became an important center for discreet diplomacy.","locator":"story paragraphs 57-71","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"The UN is a strong independent source for the existence and reported effects of the agreement and for the praise directed at Türkiye's role.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"November 2022, within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"The mediation is attributable to Erdoğan and Türkiye at the diplomatic level, but it depended on Russia, Ukraine, and UN cooperation.","contrary_evidence":["The agreement was multilateral and war-dependent, so Türkiye was necessary but not sufficient for the outcome."],"lenses":["8B.3","8B.9","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Zelensky thanks President Erdoğan for the Exchange of 215 Ukrainians with Russia","publisher":"Republic of Türkiye Directorate of Communications","publication_date":"2022-09-22","url":"https://www.iletisim.gov.tr/english/haberler/detay/zelensky-thanks-president-erdogan-for-the-exchange-of-215-ukrainians-with-russia","claim":"Ukraine's president thanked Erdoğan for the return of 215 Ukrainians after a prisoner exchange with Russia conducted thanks to Türkiye's mediation, and said five returned commanders would be under Erdoğan's close supervision in Türkiye.","locator":"paragraphs 48-65","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official Turkish communication quoting and summarizing foreign counterpart thanks; good for the fact of mediation, but still not an independent audit of bargaining strength.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"September 2022, within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Erdoğan at the diplomatic level, though the swap also depended on Russian and Ukrainian decisions.","contrary_evidence":["The exchange was a negotiated multilateral transaction, not a unilateral Turkish achievement."],"lenses":["8B.3","8B.9","8B.10"]}

**Search and Rejection Summary**
I reviewed roughly 30 documents across SBB planning pages, Invest.gov summaries, CBRT releases, IMF and World Bank reports, TÜİK data-portal pages, UN and Reuters/NATO diplomacy coverage, and several Reuters mirrors or syndication pages. I kept sources that directly established the 2022 program, concrete allocations, implementation, measurable outcomes, or ruler-linked diplomacy. I rejected duplicate mirror versions of the same Reuters stories, general governance or rights articles that did not establish execution of Erdoğan's 2022 program, and JS-gated statistics pages unless the search snippet supplied the needed official numbers. Some 2023 retrospective reports were used only because they reported 2022 outcomes.

**Remaining Gaps**
- No internal memo, cabinet minute, or presidential instruction shows Erdoğan personally authored every priority or monitored execution step.
- Project-level completion evidence is thin; the investment program shows allocation and priority, not audited completion.
- Macro outcomes are still confounded by the war in Ukraine, energy and food shocks, the post-pandemic rebound, tourism, and the inherited currency/inflation problem.
- More search would help on audited project completion, direct presidential speeches about 2022 implementation milestones, and independent evaluation of the FX-protected deposit scheme and other emergency measures.
